<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Sporitelna fund Cesky Q1 profit up.</title>
<headline>Czech Sporitelna fund Cesky Q1 profit up.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for three month period ending March 31, 1997, according to Czech accounting standards (in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Gross profit		  575.79	 vs	  283.32</p>
<p>Profit from financial</p>
<p> operations		    625.38	 vs	  339.53</p>
<p> Operating profit	    -49.59(loss) vs	  -56.21 (loss)</p>
<p> Total assets	     10,846.54	 vs     11,245.87</p>
<p> Basic capital	     7,735.46	 vs	7,735.46</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Sporitelni Privatizacni Investicni Fond - Cesky a.s.  SPIFCi.PR. The fund is managed by the investment arm of bank Ceska Sporitelna a.s.. Its shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange (PSE). Results were provided by the PSE. Midland Bank plc holds a 30 percent stake in the fund. Sporitelna holds a 25 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
